WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.968
After Emperor Wu of Jin died, his son Emperor Hui was very foolish, and court affairs were all controlled by Empress Jia Nanfeng.

00:00:08.318 --> 00:00:16.190
The eight princes, each holding great military power, distrusted one another and glared at each other all day in a tense atmosphere.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.364
Each man clenched his fists, and none was willing to step back first.

00:00:21.714 --> 00:00:28.674
To fight for the throne, they each raised armies of their own and began attacking one another.

00:00:29.024 --> 00:00:35.408
This civil war lasted a full sixteen years; the people were displaced and suffered beyond words.

00:00:35.758 --> 00:00:40.534
Many villages stood completely empty, and laughter was heard there no more.

00:00:40.884 --> 00:00:47.748
After the fires of war the palace lay in ruins; the Western Jin dynasty was gravely weakened and could never return to what it had been.

00:00:48.098 --> 00:00:53.882
Not long after the War of the Eight Princes ended, the once-mighty Western Jin moved toward its fall.

00:00:54.232 --> 00:01:00.064
This story reminds us that infighting only makes a country weaker.

